 all day so it's a damn shame they can't even go enjoy the day at the park with their friends anymore because a certain group of people refuse to act civilized and slowly but surely ruin every single thing for everybody.", "author": "RandomDude25", "created": 1791134466242, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "RandomDude25", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "For any of you that have an amusement park near your house, has your park also had to implement a chaperone policy? And if so, am I correct that it was likely due to \"teens\"?", "last_comment_created": 1791149541817, "content": "<p>It wasn't all that long ago, parents in my area\nused to buy their kids season passes for the summer and would drop them off in the morning to spend the day at the park with their friends and pick them up in the evening. Now even that has been ruined. Recurring fights and even gunshots in the park made it so kids that actually know how they behave themselves have to basically have a hall monitor with them because others don't know how to act like human beings. Teenagers don't want their parents hanging over their shoulders all day so it's a damn shame they can't even go enjoy the day at the park with their friends anymore because a certain group of people refuse to act civilized and slowly but surely ruin every single thing for everybody.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 14, "score_up": 58, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "21